+ ## Security FAQ
+ ### Q: Does MoltGuard send my sensitive data to the cloud?
+ **A: No. All sensitive data is sanitized locally before any cloud transmission.**
+ - **Component #1 (Gateway)**: 100% local, never sends data to OpenGuardrails
+ - **Component #2 (Detection)**: Sanitizes locally first, then sends only sanitized metadata to cloud
+ Example:
+ - **Local (before cloud)**: `curl https://api.internal.com -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-abc123'`
+ - **Cloud (what OpenGuardrails sees)**: `curl <URL> -H 'Authorization: Bearer <SECRET>'`
+ ### Q: Is this a man-in-the-middle attack?
+ **A: No. The AI Security Gateway is a local proxy you control that routes to YOUR LLM provider, not to OpenGuardrails.**
+ - Gateway runs on `localhost:38790` (your machine)
+ - Data flows: Your Agent → Local Gateway → **Your LLM Provider** (not OpenGuardrails)
+ - Equivalent to running a local firewall or content filter
+ - You can disable it anytime, audit the source code, or monitor network traffic
+ ### Q: What data does OpenGuardrails Core receive?
+ **A: Only sanitized metadata for security detection.**
+ **Sent to cloud:**
+ - Tool names (e.g., `"bash"`, `"read_file"`)
+ - Sanitized parameters (e.g., `<URL>`, `<SECRET>`, `<EMAIL>`)
+ - Agent intent (e.g., `"Fetch user data from API"`)
+ **NOT sent to cloud:**
+ - Original API keys, passwords, tokens
+ - Email addresses, phone numbers, SSNs
+ - File contents, source code
+ - Internal URLs, IP addresses
+ ### Q: How can I verify this claim?
+ **A: Multiple verification methods:**
+ 1. **Source code audit**: Review `moltguard/agent/sanitizer.ts` on GitHub
+ 2. **Network monitoring**: Use `tcpdump` to capture and inspect traffic
+ 3. **Package inspection**: Use `npm pack` to extract and compare with GitHub source
+ 4. **Test environment**: Install in isolated environment and monitor all connections
+ See "Trust Decision Checklist" section for detailed verification steps.
+ ### Q: Why use cloud detection instead of all-local?
+ **A: Security detection requires specialized LLMs and threat intelligence.**
+ - Prompt injection patterns evolve constantly
+ - Cross-agent threat detection requires centralized analysis
+ - Local LLM would be expensive and slow
+ - Your sensitive data is sanitized locally before cloud transmission
+ ### Q: Can I use MoltGuard without cloud detection?
+ **A: Not currently. Detection requires the cloud API.**
+ However:
+ - All data is sanitized locally before transmission
+ - You can audit the sanitization logic in `agent/sanitizer.ts`
+ - Detection API calls are fail-open (network issues don't block your work)
+ - You control when to register and can revoke credentials anytime
+ ### Q: What happens if I don't trust the sanitization?
+ **A: Don't install. MoltGuard requires trust in the local sanitization logic.**
+ Before installing:
+ 1. Review `moltguard/agent/sanitizer.ts` source code
+ 2. Verify package provenance (`npm view @openguardrails/moltguard repository.url`)
+ 3. Test in isolated environment with network monitoring
+ 4. Only install if you trust the sanitization implementation
+ If you find any issues, please report them on GitHub: https://github.com/openguardrails/openguardrails/issues